[38;5;252m[1m## Behaviours deliberately preserved, not fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mwhile (getchar() != '\n')[0m after a failed [38;5;10mscanf[0m loops forever at EOF ([38;5;10mgetchar[0m returns EOF, never [38;5;10m'\n'[0m). Reproduced literally, so the Rust binary hangs on exactly the same inputs the C does.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mscanf("%d")[0m overflow follows glibc: values saturate at [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m, then truncate to [38;5;10mint[0m, so [38;5;10m99999999999999999999[0m becomes [38;5;10m-1[0m.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mscene_load[0m fails silently (no message) on a malformed shape count, and silently skips out-of-range shape types.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstrncpy[0m truncation of scene names to 63 bytes; [38;5;10mfgets[0m splitting of menu lines longer than 255 bytes.[0m[0m
- stdout is fully buffered at 4096 bytes with stderr unbuffered, matching glibc when stdout is a pipe, so the interleaving of [38;5;10mError: Scene is full[0m with normal output is preserved.[0m[0m
