One irreducible caveat: [38;5;10m%p[0m output. The C program prints raw heap addresses, which are ASLR-randomized and differ between two runs of the C binary itself, so byte-identical pointer text is not achievable. I matched everything that is deterministic — the [38;5;10mShape[0m struct is [38;5;10m#[repr(C)][0m at exactly 2444 bytes and the ten allocations are made back-to-back, so the [3mstride[23m between printed pointers is 0x56A0 in both binaries. Only the base address differs. Comparisons that normalize hex addresses match exactly; comparisons that don't will differ on pointer lines for the C binary too.[0m[0m
